1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:02,780
Look closely.

2
00:00:03,080 --> 00:00:04,320
A cockroach.

3
00:00:04,380 --> 00:00:05,120
A giant,

4
00:00:04,820 --> 00:00:06,020
by any measure,

5
00:00:05,720 --> 00:00:07,760
next to the creatures around it.

6
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:08,280
And yet,

7
00:00:07,980 --> 00:00:08,980
one by one,

8
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:10,200
then dozens at a time,

9
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:11,180
the ants arrive.

10
00:00:11,740 --> 00:00:13,700
How is that even possible?

11
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:15,740
The ants are not stronger.

12
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:18,160
Not one of them could win this alone.

13
00:00:18,260 --> 00:00:20,140
But none of them is alone.

14
00:00:20,760 --> 00:00:22,400
When the little ones come together,

15
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:23,700
even giants fall.

16
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:25,100
This is the mystery,

17
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:25,900
and the magic,

18
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:27,020
of the ant kingdom.

19
00:00:27,620 --> 00:00:28,940
Start with the numbers,

20
00:00:28,640 --> 00:00:31,000
because the numbers are hard to believe.

21
00:00:31,540 --> 00:00:32,820
In 2022,

22
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:35,680
a team of scientists gathered nearly five hundred

23
00:00:35,380 --> 00:00:36,740
studies of ants,

24
00:00:36,440 --> 00:00:39,380
from every continent and every major habitat,

25
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:40,440
and they counted.

26
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:41,400
Their estimate:

27
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:44,220
about twenty quadrillion ants alive on Earth right

28
00:00:43,920 --> 00:00:44,640
now.

29
00:00:44,660 --> 00:00:45,540
A twenty,

30
00:00:45,240 --> 00:00:47,300
followed by fifteen zeros.

31
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:50,140
And they called that number conservative.

32
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:52,720
That is roughly two and a half million

33
00:00:52,420 --> 00:00:55,060
ants for every human being on the planet.

34
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:56,420
Put them all on a scale,

35
00:00:56,120 --> 00:00:58,860
and ants outweigh every wild bird and every

36
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:00,040
wild mammal on Earth,

37
00:00:59,740 --> 00:01:00,760
combined.

38
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:04,260
Scientists have named more than twelve thousand species.

39
00:01:04,580 --> 00:01:07,500
They live on every continent except Antarctica.

40
00:01:07,840 --> 00:01:09,620
They were here long before us,

41
00:01:09,320 --> 00:01:11,660
and they have been working together the entire

42
00:01:11,360 --> 00:01:12,160
time.

43
00:01:12,680 --> 00:01:14,380
So here is the question.

44
00:01:14,700 --> 00:01:15,960
Who is in charge?

45
00:01:16,480 --> 00:01:19,080
The answer is the strangest part of the

46
00:01:18,780 --> 00:01:19,480
story.

47
00:01:19,180 --> 00:01:20,760
Nobody.

48
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:23,320
The queen does not give orders.

49
00:01:23,780 --> 00:01:24,780
She lays eggs.

50
00:01:25,060 --> 00:01:26,260
That is her job,

51
00:01:25,960 --> 00:01:27,440
and it is a big one.

52
00:01:27,520 --> 00:01:29,460
But she does not command an army,

53
00:01:29,160 --> 00:01:31,140
and she does not draw a plan.

54
00:01:31,820 --> 00:01:32,500
Instead,

55
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:34,360
the colony runs on signals.

56
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:37,560
Ants talk through chemicals called pheromones.

57
00:01:37,880 --> 00:01:39,420
When a worker finds food,

58
00:01:39,120 --> 00:01:41,200
she lays a scent trail on the way

59
00:01:40,900 --> 00:01:41,560
home.

60
00:01:41,760 --> 00:01:43,580
Other workers follow it.

61
00:01:43,560 --> 00:01:44,760
If the food is good,

62
00:01:44,460 --> 00:01:45,780
they lay trail too,

63
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:47,460
and the path grows stronger.

64
00:01:47,620 --> 00:01:49,020
When the food runs out,

65
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:50,760
nobody reinforces the trail,

66
00:01:50,460 --> 00:01:51,920
and it fades away.

67
00:01:52,460 --> 00:01:53,500
No meeting.

68
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:54,800
No memo.

69
00:01:54,900 --> 00:01:57,120
The best route simply gets louder.

70
00:01:57,460 --> 00:01:59,260
And when danger appears,

71
00:01:58,960 --> 00:02:00,900
a different signal goes out.

72
00:02:00,960 --> 00:02:01,840
An alarm.

73
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:04,380
What started as a few workers can become

74
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:05,500
dozens in minutes.

75
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:07,620
Then there are the tools.

76
00:02:08,080 --> 00:02:09,860
Ants carry them on their faces.

77
00:02:10,180 --> 00:02:11,900
They are called mandibles.

78
00:02:12,340 --> 00:02:13,240
Jaws that grip,

79
00:02:12,940 --> 00:02:13,560
bite,

80
00:02:13,260 --> 00:02:14,500
cut and carry.

81
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:16,840
One set of mandibles is small.

82
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:18,240
A thousand sets,

83
00:02:17,940 --> 00:02:19,580
working the same target,

84
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:20,600
are something else.

85
00:02:21,160 --> 00:02:23,040
That is what you are seeing in that

86
00:02:22,740 --> 00:02:23,400
video.

87
00:02:23,660 --> 00:02:24,240
Often,

88
00:02:23,940 --> 00:02:26,760
the insect is already weakened or injured.

89
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:29,080
The ants do not need to be bigger.

90
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:30,820
They only need to be more,

91
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:32,300
and they need to move as one.

92
00:02:32,860 --> 00:02:34,960
Scientists have a name for this.

93
00:02:35,120 --> 00:02:36,320
Collective behavior.

94
00:02:36,760 --> 00:02:38,440
Each ant follows simple,

95
00:02:38,140 --> 00:02:39,400
local rules.

96
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:40,220
Together,

97
00:02:39,920 --> 00:02:43,120
the colony solves problems that no single ant

98
00:02:42,820 --> 00:02:44,180
could ever understand.

99
00:02:44,720 --> 00:02:46,820
To see how far that idea goes,

100
00:02:46,760 --> 00:02:48,320
open four case files.

101
00:02:49,180 --> 00:02:50,420
Case file one.

102
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:51,520
The army.

103
00:02:52,020 --> 00:02:54,820
In the rainforests of Central and South America,

104
00:02:54,960 --> 00:02:57,760
one species of army ant lives in colonies

105
00:02:57,460 --> 00:02:59,540
of hundreds of thousands of workers.

106
00:02:59,700 --> 00:03:01,620
They have no permanent home.

107
00:03:01,820 --> 00:03:02,560
Each night,

108
00:03:02,260 --> 00:03:03,260
they build one,

109
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:04,500
out of their own bodies,

110
00:03:04,540 --> 00:03:07,200
linking legs and jaws into a living nest

111
00:03:06,900 --> 00:03:08,040
around their queen.

112
00:03:07,740 --> 00:03:09,980
They call it a bivouac.

113
00:03:10,360 --> 00:03:11,160
By day,

114
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:11,780
they raid.

115
00:03:11,980 --> 00:03:14,200
A swarm front up to ten meters wide

116
00:03:13,900 --> 00:03:15,780
sweeps across the forest floor,

117
00:03:15,980 --> 00:03:18,440
and almost everything small in its path either

118
00:03:18,140 --> 00:03:20,120
runs or is carried away.

119
00:03:20,760 --> 00:03:22,160
Case file two.

120
00:03:22,440 --> 00:03:23,380
The farmers.

121
00:03:23,080 --> 00:03:26,980
Long before human beings planted a single seed,

122
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:28,060
ants were farming.

123
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:30,180
By many scientific estimates,

124
00:03:30,240 --> 00:03:33,360
ants began growing fungus around fifty million years

125
00:03:33,060 --> 00:03:33,720
ago.

126
00:03:34,260 --> 00:03:37,120
Leafcutter ants carry pieces of leaves back home,

127
00:03:37,160 --> 00:03:38,160
not to eat them,

128
00:03:38,080 --> 00:03:40,460
but to feed underground gardens of fungus.

129
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:42,840
The fungus feeds the colony.

130
00:03:43,140 --> 00:03:45,160
The colony tends the fungus.

131
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:46,360
A partnership,

132
00:03:46,060 --> 00:03:48,560
older than any human civilization.

133
00:03:49,540 --> 00:03:50,800
Case file three.

134
00:03:51,080 --> 00:03:51,880
The raft.

135
00:03:52,580 --> 00:03:53,660
When floods come,

136
00:03:53,620 --> 00:03:56,140
a single fire ant struggles in the water.

137
00:03:56,200 --> 00:03:58,620
But a colony does something remarkable.

138
00:03:58,860 --> 00:04:00,960
The ants grip each other with their claws,

139
00:04:01,020 --> 00:04:03,140
their jaws and the pads on their feet,

140
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:05,520
and they weave themselves into a living raft.

141
00:04:06,140 --> 00:04:06,860
Thousands of them,

142
00:04:06,560 --> 00:04:07,700
floating together,

143
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:09,780
with the queen and the young kept safe

144
00:04:09,480 --> 00:04:10,340
on board.

145
00:04:10,700 --> 00:04:13,400
Researchers have watched these rafts stay afloat for

146
00:04:13,100 --> 00:04:13,780
days,

147
00:04:13,820 --> 00:04:14,740
even weeks.

148
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:17,080
No ant built that raft.

149
00:04:17,420 --> 00:04:19,140
Every ant is the raft.

150
00:04:19,940 --> 00:04:21,140
Case file four.

151
00:04:20,840 --> 00:04:22,260
The empire.

152
00:04:22,920 --> 00:04:25,020
A little brown ant from South America,

153
00:04:25,020 --> 00:04:26,420
the Argentine ant,

154
00:04:26,320 --> 00:04:28,660
arrived in Europe about a century ago,

155
00:04:28,660 --> 00:04:29,900
probably on ships.

156
00:04:30,220 --> 00:04:30,800
Today,

157
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:33,640
one of its supercolonies stretches about six thousand

158
00:04:33,340 --> 00:04:35,000
kilometers along the coast,

159
00:04:35,100 --> 00:04:37,640
from Italy to the Atlantic coast of Spain.

160
00:04:38,320 --> 00:04:39,960
Inside that supercolony,

161
00:04:40,060 --> 00:04:43,000
ants from nests thousands of kilometers apart treat

162
00:04:42,700 --> 00:04:44,060
each other as family.

163
00:04:44,260 --> 00:04:45,580
They do not fight.

164
00:04:45,620 --> 00:04:47,540
But when they meet ants from a rival

165
00:04:47,240 --> 00:04:48,340
supercolony,

166
00:04:48,360 --> 00:04:49,620
they fight to the death.

167
00:04:50,240 --> 00:04:51,480
Think about that.

168
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:54,660
One of the largest cooperative societies in Europe

169
00:04:54,360 --> 00:04:56,880
is made entirely of little ones.

170
00:04:57,540 --> 00:04:59,300
So what does all of this mean for

171
00:04:59,000 --> 00:04:59,680
us?

172
00:05:00,160 --> 00:05:02,660
The biggest creature does not always win.

173
00:05:02,840 --> 00:05:05,920
The strongest individual does not always survive.

174
00:05:06,120 --> 00:05:08,700
And having every advantage in the world means

175
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:10,840
very little when you are facing a united,

176
00:05:10,840 --> 00:05:12,060
organized force.

177
00:05:12,720 --> 00:05:14,660
Think about that in your community.

178
00:05:14,940 --> 00:05:16,000
In your family.

179
00:05:16,320 --> 00:05:17,460
In your business.

180
00:05:17,720 --> 00:05:20,440
In any movement that ever changed anything.

181
00:05:21,020 --> 00:05:23,320
Nobody needs to see the whole mission.

182
00:05:23,560 --> 00:05:25,560
Each one only needs to do their part,

183
00:05:25,580 --> 00:05:26,700
follow the signal,

184
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:28,900
and hold on to the ones beside them.

185
00:05:29,340 --> 00:05:30,940
One ant is small.

186
00:05:31,180 --> 00:05:33,140
A thousand ants are a force.

187
00:05:33,940 --> 00:05:37,020
Nature keeps reminding us that unity can turn

188
00:05:36,720 --> 00:05:38,600
the powerless into the powerful.

189
00:05:39,200 --> 00:05:41,540
And maybe that is the real magic.

190
00:05:41,700 --> 00:05:43,820
Not that the little ones can bring down

191
00:05:43,520 --> 00:05:44,340
a giant.

192
00:05:44,540 --> 00:05:45,600
But that together,

193
00:05:45,300 --> 00:05:48,060
they become something much bigger than themselves.

194
00:05:48,780 --> 00:05:50,000
The Ant Kingdom.

195
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:52,160
Produced by Relentless Aaron.

